<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<databaseChangeLog
  xmlns="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog"
  xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
  xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog/dbchangelog-3.8.xsd">

  <!--
    DH-011P (Design B, LIBAN DECISION: SELECT DESIGN B, patches/order-correlation/PROVENANCE.md):
    a standalone table for the per-added-test DH-025 correlation. Deliberately not a column on
    clinlims.analysis and not a second row shape on electronic_order - both DH-011O blockers
    this closes are that those two mechanisms are scalar-per-object and cannot represent
    independent, repeatable "add a test to an existing accession" events without breaking the
    original order's own correlation semantics.

    Columns beyond the ticket's stated minimum (id, analysis_id, correlation_value, created_at):
    last_updated is required by org.openelisglobal.common.valueholder.BaseObject, which every
    entity reachable through this codebase's shared BaseDAO/BaseObjectService infrastructure
    extends and which unconditionally maps a @Version column named last_updated. This table is
    insert-only (no UPDATE ever issued against it), so optimistic-lock conflicts on it are not
    expected in practice, but the column must exist for the entity to load through that shared
    infrastructure at all.

    Constraints:
      - analysis_id: NOT NULL, FK to clinlims.analysis(id), no ON DELETE action specified (the
        default, NO ACTION) - OpenELIS never hard-deletes an Analysis (status is set to
        Canceled instead), and this migration must not silently lose correlation/audit evidence
        by cascading a delete that upstream itself does not perform.
      - correlation_value: NOT NULL, exactly 64 lowercase hex characters (see
        DaherOrderCorrelation.VALUE_PATTERN for the Java-side twin of this constraint), UNIQUE.
      - analysis_id is NOT unique in this changeset. It was left non-unique here for a real,
        source-verified reason (SampleEditServiceImpl.newOrExistingCanceledAnalysis revives a
        cancelled Analysis on a matching re-add rather than inserting a new one, so one Analysis
        could otherwise legitimately be the target of two add-events across its lifecycle). Liban
        reviewed that tradeoff (DH-011P3) and chose the strict one-Analysis-one-correlation
        invariant instead, accepting that a Daher re-add after native cancellation now fails
        loudly rather than reviving. See 005-daher-analysis-correlation-unique-analysis.xml,
        which supersedes this decision and adds the unique constraint - do not treat this
        changeset's index as the final word on analysis_id uniqueness.

    Fails safely, not destructively: if this table or its objects already exist under a name
    this migration collides with, CREATE fails and Liquibase does not mark the changeset applied.
    No existing data is read, rewritten, or backfilled - there is no historical "add a test"
    event to reconstruct a correlation for, and this migration does not attempt to invent one.
  -->
  <changeSet id="daher-011p-004-daher-analysis-correlation" author="daher-health">
    <sql>
      CREATE SEQUENCE daher_analysis_correlation_seq;

      CREATE TABLE daher_analysis_correlation (
        id BIGINT PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT nextval('daher_analysis_correlation_seq'),
        analysis_id NUMERIC(10,0) NOT NULL
          REFERENCES clinlims.analysis (id),
        correlation_value VARCHAR(64) NOT NULL
          CONSTRAINT daher_analysis_correlation_value_format
          CHECK (correlation_value ~ '^[0-9a-f]{64}$'),
        created_at TIMESTAMP NOT NULL DEFAULT now(),
        last_updated TIMESTAMP NOT NULL DEFAULT now()
      );

      ALTER SEQUENCE daher_analysis_correlation_seq OWNED BY daher_analysis_correlation.id;

      CREATE UNIQUE INDEX daher_analysis_correlation_value_uk
        ON daher_analysis_correlation (correlation_value);

      CREATE INDEX daher_analysis_correlation_analysis_idx
        ON daher_analysis_correlation (analysis_id);
    </sql>
    <rollback>
      <sql>
        DROP TABLE IF EXISTS daher_analysis_correlation;
        DROP SEQUENCE IF EXISTS daher_analysis_correlation_seq;
      </sql>
    </rollback>
  </changeSet>
</databaseChangeLog>
